{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019YywJQ2GVMN9PEihkrxNzm","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Employee CRUD REST API — AS-IS Spring 4 Legacy Stack\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→A traditional Spring MVC REST API for employee management.\n     5→This is an **AS-IS legacy project** to be used as migration tool input.\n     6→\n     7→- **Java 1.8** (source/target compatibility 1.8)\n     8→- **Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE** (NOT Spring Boot — uses XML/Java config)\n     9→- **Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE** (form-based + basic auth)\n    10→- **MyBatis 3.2.2** (XML mapper files)\n    11→- **PostgreSQL** (JDBC via commons-dbcp2 connection pool)\n    12→- **Maven** build system\n    13→- **Embedded Tomcat 8.5** for integration tests (maven-tomcat7-plugin or embedded server)\n    14→- **JUnit 4** + Mockito for testing\n    15→\n    16→## Functional Requirements\n    17→\n    18→### Entity: Employee\n    19→| Field       | Type      | Constraints                       |\n    20→|-------------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n    21→| id          | Long      | PK, auto-increment                |\n    22→| name        | String    | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars             |\n    23→| email       | String    | NOT NULL, unique, valid email     |\n    24→| department  | String    | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars              |\n    25→| salary      | BigDecimal| NOT NULL, >= 0                    |\n    26→| hireDate    | Date      | NOT NULL                          |\n    27→| createdAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert                |\n    28→| updatedAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update         |\n    29→\n    30→### REST Endpoints\n    31→| Method | Path                   | Description           | Auth Required |\n    32→|--------|------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|\n    33→| GET    | /api/employees         | List all (paginated)  | USER role     |\n    34→| GET    | /api/employees/{id}    | Get by ID             | USER role     |\n    35→| POST   | /api/employees         | Create new            | ADMIN role    |\n    36→| PUT    | /api/employees/{id}    | Update existing       | ADMIN role    |\n    37→| DELETE | /api/employees/{id}    | Delete                | ADMIN role    |\n    38→| GET    | /api/employees/search  | Search by name/dept   | USER role     |\n    39→\n    40→### Pagination\n    41→- Query params: `page` (0-based), `size` (default 10, max 100)\n    42→- Response wraps list with `totalPages`, `totalElements`, `currentPage`\n    43→\n    44→### Authentication & Authorization\n    45→- Spring Security 4.2.4 with HTTP Basic Auth for API endpoints\n    46→- In-memory user store (for demo purposes):\n    47→  - `admin` / `admin123` → role ADMIN\n    48→  - `user` / `user123` → role USER\n    49→- CSRF disabled for REST API\n    50→- Stateless session (no cookies)\n    51→\n    52→### Error Handling\n    53→- 400 for validation errors (with field-level detail)\n    54→- 404 for not-found\n    55→- 409 for duplicate email\n    56→- 401/403 for auth failures\n    57→- Standard error response: `{ \"status\": 400, \"error\": \"Bad Request\", \"message\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }`\n    58→\n    59→## Architecture\n    60→\n    61→```\n    62→com.example.legacy/\n    63→├── config/\n    64→│   ├── AppConfig.java          # Root Spring config (component scan, property source)\n    65→│   ├── WebConfig.java          # Spring MVC config (message converters, CORS)\n    66→│   ├── SecurityConfig.java     # Spring Security config\n    67→│   ├── DatabaseConfig.java     # DataSource + SqlSessionFactory + Transaction\n    68→│   └── WebInitializer.java     # AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer\n    69→├── model/\n    70→│   ├── Employee.java           # Entity POJO\n    71→│   └── PageResult.java         # Pagination wrapper\n    72→├── mapper/\n    73→│   └── EmployeeMapper.java     # MyBatis mapper interface\n    74→├── service/\n    75→│   ├── EmployeeService.java    # Interface\n    76→│   └── EmployeeServiceImpl.java # Implementation\n    77→├── controller/\n    78→│   ├── EmployeeController.java # REST controller\n    79→│   └── GlobalExceptionHandler.java # @ControllerAdvice\n    80→├── dto/\n    81→│   ├── EmployeeRequest.java    # Input DTO with validation\n    82→│   └── ErrorResponse.java      # Error response DTO\n    83→└── validation/\n    84→    └── EmployeeValidator.java  # Manual bean validation (javax.validation)\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→### MyBatis XML Mappers\n    88→`src/main/resources/mapper/EmployeeMapper.xml` — all SQL in XML:\n    89→- `findAll` with LIMIT/OFFSET\n    90→- `findById`\n    91→- `insert` with `useGeneratedKeys`\n    92→- `update`\n    93→- `delete`\n    94→- `countAll`\n    95→- `searchByNameOrDepartment` with LIKE\n    96→- `findByEmail`\n    97→\n    98→### Configuration Files\n    99→- `src/main/resources/application.properties` — DB connection, MyBatis settings\n   100→- `src/main/resources/schema.sql` — DDL for employees table\n   101→- `src/main/resources/data.sql` — seed data (5 sample employees)\n   102→- `src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml` — (optional, since using Java config)\n   103→\n   104→## Non-Functional Requirements\n   105→- **Java 1.8 compatible** — no lambdas only if absolutely needed, prefer anonymous classes where possible for legacy feel, but lambdas are OK since Java 8 supports them\n   106→- All dependencies managed in `pom.xml` with explicit versions\n   107→- No Spring Boot auto-configuration — everything manually configured\n   108→- Log with SLF4J + Logback\n   109→- Unit tests with JUnit 4 + Mockito\n   110→- Integration tests using Spring Test with H2 in-memory DB (test profile)\n   111→\n   112→## Testing Requirements\n   113→- `tests/` mapped to `src/test/java/com/example/legacy/`\n   114→- Unit tests for Service layer (mock mapper)\n   115→- Unit tests for Controller layer (MockMvc)\n   116→- Integration tests with Spring TestContext + H2\n   117→- Target: at least 15 test methods across test classes\n   118→\n   119→## Build & Run\n   120→```bash\n   121→# Build\n   122→mvn clean compile\n   123→\n   124→# Test (uses H2 in-memory)\n   125→mvn test\n   126→\n   127→# Package\n   128→mvn clean package\n   129→\n   130→# Run with embedded Tomcat (if configured) or deploy WAR to Tomcat\n   131→mvn tomcat7:run    # or use exec-maven-plugin with embedded server\n   132→```\n   133→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d91a04ba-28f5-42f6-876a-7c37ccdcf343","uuid":"de85aef1-4628-4432-92d4-892f6600e692","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/specs/employee-crud-api.md","content":"# Employee CRUD REST API — AS-IS Spring 4 Legacy Stack\n\n## Overview\nA traditional Spring MVC REST API for employee management.\nThis is an **AS-IS legacy project** to be used as migration tool input.\n\n- **Java 1.8** (source/target compatibility 1.8)\n- **Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE** (NOT Spring Boot — uses XML/Java config)\n- **Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE** (form-based + basic auth)\n- **MyBatis 3.2.2** (XML mapper files)\n- **PostgreSQL** (JDBC via commons-dbcp2 connection pool)\n- **Maven** build system\n- **Embedded Tomcat 8.5** for integration tests (maven-tomcat7-plugin or embedded server)\n- **JUnit 4** + Mockito for testing\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Entity: Employee\n| Field       | Type      | Constraints                       |\n|-------------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n| id          | Long      | PK, auto-increment                |\n| name        | String    | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars             |\n| email       | String    | NOT NULL, unique, valid email     |\n| department  | String    | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars              |\n| salary      | BigDecimal| NOT NULL, >= 0                    |\n| hireDate    | Date      | NOT NULL                          |\n| createdAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert                |\n| updatedAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update         |\n\n### REST Endpoints\n| Method | Path                   | Description           | Auth Required |\n|--------|------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|\n| GET    | /api/employees         | List all (paginated)  | USER role     |\n| GET    | /api/employees/{id}    | Get by ID             | USER role     |\n| POST   | /api/employees         | Create new            | ADMIN role    |\n| PUT    | /api/employees/{id}    | Update existing       | ADMIN role    |\n| DELETE | /api/employees/{id}    | Delete                | ADMIN role    |\n| GET    | /api/employees/search  | Search by name/dept   | USER role     |\n\n### Pagination\n- Query params: `page` (0-based), `size` (default 10, max 100)\n- Response wraps list with `totalPages`, `totalElements`, `currentPage`\n\n### Authentication & Authorization\n- Spring Security 4.2.4 with HTTP Basic Auth for API endpoints\n- In-memory user store (for demo purposes):\n  - `admin` / `admin123` → role ADMIN\n  - `user` / `user123` → role USER\n- CSRF disabled for REST API\n- Stateless session (no cookies)\n\n### Error Handling\n- 400 for validation errors (with field-level detail)\n- 404 for not-found\n- 409 for duplicate email\n- 401/403 for auth failures\n- Standard error response: `{ \"status\": 400, \"error\": \"Bad Request\", \"message\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }`\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\ncom.example.legacy/\n├── config/\n│   ├── AppConfig.java          # Root Spring config (component scan, property source)\n│   ├── WebConfig.java          # Spring MVC config (message converters, CORS)\n│   ├── SecurityConfig.java     # Spring Security config\n│   ├── DatabaseConfig.java     # DataSource + SqlSessionFactory + Transaction\n│   └── WebInitializer.java     # AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer\n├── model/\n│   ├── Employee.java           # Entity POJO\n│   └── PageResult.java         # Pagination wrapper\n├── mapper/\n│   └── EmployeeMapper.java     # MyBatis mapper interface\n├── service/\n│   ├── EmployeeService.java    # Interface\n│   └── EmployeeServiceImpl.java # Implementation\n├── controller/\n│   ├── EmployeeController.java # REST controller\n│   └── GlobalExceptionHandler.java # @ControllerAdvice\n├── dto/\n│   ├── EmployeeRequest.java    # Input DTO with validation\n│   └── ErrorResponse.java      # Error response DTO\n└── validation/\n    └── EmployeeValidator.java  # Manual bean validation (javax.validation)\n```\n\n### MyBatis XML Mappers\n`src/main/resources/mapper/EmployeeMapper.xml` — all SQL in XML:\n- `findAll` with LIMIT/OFFSET\n- `findById`\n- `insert` with `useGeneratedKeys`\n- `update`\n- `delete`\n- `countAll`\n- `searchByNameOrDepartment` with LIKE\n- `findByEmail`\n\n### Configuration Files\n- `src/main/resources/application.properties` — DB connection, MyBatis settings\n- `src/main/resources/schema.sql` — DDL for employees table\n- `src/main/resources/data.sql` — seed data (5 sample employees)\n- `src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml` — (optional, since using Java config)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **Java 1.8 compatible** — no lambdas only if absolutely needed, prefer anonymous classes where possible for legacy feel, but lambdas are OK since Java 8 supports them\n- All dependencies managed in `pom.xml` with explicit versions\n- No Spring Boot auto-configuration — everything manually configured\n- Log with SLF4J + Logback\n- Unit tests with JUnit 4 + Mockito\n- Integration tests using Spring Test with H2 in-memory DB (test profile)\n\n## Testing Requirements\n- `tests/` mapped to `src/test/java/com/example/legacy/`\n- Unit tests for Service layer (mock mapper)\n- Unit tests for Controller layer (MockMvc)\n- Integration tests with Spring TestContext + H2\n- Target: at least 15 test methods across test classes\n\n## Build & Run\n```bash\n# Build\nmvn clean compile\n\n# Test (uses H2 in-memory)\nmvn test\n\n# Package\nmvn clean package\n\n# Run with embedded Tomcat (if configured) or deploy WAR to Tomcat\nmvn tomcat7:run    # or use exec-maven-plugin with embedded server\n```\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019dK1Z1YAgWzCaUWrpABCAh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. I need to implement Item 4: Spring application and database configuration. The spec shows the architecture:\n\n```\ncom.example.legacy/\n├── config/\n│   ├── AppConfig.java          # Root Spring config (component scan, property source)\n│   ├── WebConfig.java          # Spring MVC config (message converters, CORS)\n│   ├── SecurityConfig.java     # Spring Security config\n│   ├── DatabaseConfig.java     # DataSource + SqlSessionFactory + Transaction\n│   └── WebInitializer.java     # AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer\n\n\n```\n\nI need to create AppConfig with component scanning and property source loading, then set up DatabaseConfig with a Commons DBCP2 DataSource, SqlSessionFactory configured with the Employee type alias and mapper locations, and a MapperScannerConfigurer to auto-wire mappers from the mapper package. The production properties file will contain PostgreSQL connection defaults.\n\nI should also verify whether WebConfig and WebInitializer are required for this item or if they're separate components. Looking at the acceptance criteria, it focuses specifically on AppConfig, DatabaseConfig, and the properties file, so those are the core deliverables. The transaction manager needs to be wired into DatabaseConfig as well.\n\nI'll also need to check if data.sql with sample employee seed data is part of this item or handled separately.\n\n``` I need to be pragmatic here—while Item 4 explicitly specifies only AppConfig and DatabaseConfig, I also need WebConfig and WebInitializer for the application to actually compile and run, so I'll implement all four configuration classes together in the config package.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the specific configuration details: the mapper XML will live in `src/main/resources/mappers/EmployeeMapper.xml`, I need to set up type aliases for the Employee class, and configure the MapperScannerConfigurer to scan the mapper package. My approach is to create AppConfig with component scanning and property source loading, then DatabaseConfig with the database connection setup and MyBatis configuration.\n\nFor the web layer, I'll set up WebConfig with MVC enablement, Jackson serialization with timezone handling, and CORS support for development, then create WebInitializer to bootstrap the servlet context.\n\nNow I need to configure the application properties for PostgreSQL and connection pooling, then start implementing these configuration classes using @Value to inject the database properties that AppConfig loads from the property source.\n\nI'm realizing there's a dependency issue with WebInitializer—it references SecurityConfig which doesn't exist yet since that's Item 5, so I need to either defer creating WebInitializer to a later item or create it without the SecurityConfig reference for now.\n\nLooking at what Item 4 actually requires, the description focuses on AppConfig and DatabaseConfig, so I'll create those along with WebConfig and WebInitializer, but I'll structure it so SecurityConfig can be added to the root config classes later without breaking the current setup. I'll also need to set up the application.properties file with the database configuration keys. Now I'm setting up the DatabaseConfig class with MyBatis and transaction management, configuring the data source, session factory, and mapper scanner. Setting up the MyBatis configuration with a SqlSessionFactory bean that loads mapper XML files from the classpath, then configuring transaction management with a DataSourceTransactionManager, and finally setting up the mapper scanner to auto-detect and register mapper interfaces.\n\nNow I'm moving into the web configuration layer, setting up Spring MVC with Jackson for JSON serialization and configuring CORS support. Finishing up the CORS configuration to allow those HTTP methods, then setting up the servlet initializer that registers the root and web configurations to bootstrap the Spring application.\n\nNow I'm looking at the database properties file with PostgreSQL connection details and connection pool settings. I need to be careful here—the @PropertySource in AppConfig points to application.properties for production, but tests use application-test.properties with H2 instead. The test configuration will override this with its own DataSource, so there shouldn't be a conflict between the two environments. I'm realizing that MapperScannerConfigurer being a BeanDefinitionRegistryPostProcessor creates a timing issue—it runs before the ApplicationContext fully initializes, which means @Value annotations in DatabaseConfig might not resolve properly at that point. Since I'm already using `setSqlSessionFactoryBeanName` with a string reference instead of injecting the actual bean, this should avoid that problem. I'm settling on making MapperScannerConfigurer a static @Bean method, which ensures it's instantiated before other config methods run and avoids Spring's bean dependency resolution issues. Now I'll write out the complete configuration files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2582,"cache_read_input_tokens":45770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2582},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d91a04ba-28f5-42f6-876a-7c37ccdcf343","uuid":"8cfe6025-054b-456f-a59c-24a9c8cce378"}
